\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge-invariant matter observables}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Two matter fields at different vertices transform under
different changes of coefficient basis. A path between their
vertices supplies a map that can join the two indices.
Which contractions survive every vertex gauge, and what does
the finite coupled coefficient assign to them? Invariant
averages and exterior covectors give complementary
constructions, while the sign torus gives an exact value for a chosen path
and exhibits the effect of the matter determinant.}

\transclude{fdip-00WB}
